From 315664bccf05a3490a968a185abb5d89a88808b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filyus <filyus@filyus.ru>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:23:52 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: explain a tokenHelper in profile, on a 401 and when
 a helper fails to start

`profile enable-2fa` says why it cannot work through a helper. The message names
the helper only when its value is an existing file, and the config key
otherwise.

A 401 from a registry that has a helper says that the registry refused the token
the helper printed and to refresh the login or the cache of the tool behind it,
instead of suggesting `npm login`, which does not change what the helper prints.

The runner says more about why a helper could not run: a script whose #!
interpreter is missing names it (and a CRLF line ending as the likely cause),
exit status 127 or 9009 says that a tool the script calls was not found and to
give its absolute path, and a .ps1 or .js file on Windows, which Windows does
not start directly, is refused with a pointer to a .cmd wrapper.
